+# The Daily Grind — phone verification
+
+Static, responsive phone verification UI. Open `index.html` through your existing hosting environment. No build step or dependencies are needed.
+
+With an empty `verification-api-base` meta value, the page runs a clearly labeled demonstration: no SMS is sent, and `123456` completes the demo. Codes expire after five minutes. The demo does not establish verified identity.
+
+## Connect an SMS service
+
+Set the meta tag in `index.html` to your same-origin backend base path, for example:
+
+```html
+<meta name="verification-api-base" content="/api/verification">
+```
+
+Implement these JSON POST endpoints:
+
+- `/api/verification/send`: accepts `{ "phone": "+15551234567" }`; returns `{ "challengeId": "opaque-server-id", "retryAfter": 30 }` after sending the code. `retryAfter` is in seconds.
+- `/api/verification/check`: accepts `{ "challengeId": "opaque-server-id", "code": "012345" }`; returns `{ "verified": true }` only after server-side verification. Use non-2xx responses for invalid/expired codes and `429` for rate limits.
+
+The backend must generate and securely store expiring codes, bind challenges to the session and phone number, enforce attempt and resend limits, invalidate codes after use/resend, and persist verification server-side. Use same-origin sessions with secure cookies and request-origin/CSRF validation. Never use the demo code in production.
+
+Send messages in this format, with the deployed hostname (no scheme, port, or path) on the final line:
+
+```text
+Your Daily Grind verification code is 012345.
+
+@your-domain.com #012345
+```
+
+Production WebOTP requires HTTPS and browser support. It is feature detected, uses a cancellable listener started before sending the SMS, and falls back to native `one-time-code` autofill and manual entry. Requests are aborted on submission, resend, changing the number, and page exit. The code uses one text input to preserve leading zeros, pasting, and accessible navigation.
+
+Photography: [Unsplash](https://unsplash.com/photos/1442512595331-e89e73853f31) (locally saved in `assets/coffee.jpg`). Fonts: DM Sans and Manrope via Google Fonts, with system fallbacks.
